":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T05:23:30-07:00","id":919043,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11842_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11842\" data-vbnamecard=\"11842\">Aeryes</a>,<br /> <br /> A reset button has been added.<br /> <br /> Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a><br /> <br /> Gnosis has been moved to the top now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:43:44-07:00","id":919114,"title":"","content":"I've downloaded the latest version and the Advanced Scale and Advanced Duration check boxes don't seem to do anything now.<br /> <br /> In regards to Attainments, is it possible to add a box for the Fate 2 Attainment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8871-griffalo","name":"griffalo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8871_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T09:42:44-07:00","id":919141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffalo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/914782-spell-calculator?p=919114#post919114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've downloaded the latest version and the Advanced Scale and Advanced Duration check boxes don't seem to do anything now.<br /> <br /> In regards to Attainments, is it possible to add a box for the Fate 2 Attainment?</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you calculate that one automatically, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T10:07:23-07:00","id":919164,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8871-griffalo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8871_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8871\" data-vbnamecard=\"8871\">griffalo</a>,<br /> <br /> Yeah, there was a slight issue there with logic. That has been corrected and you should now see the correct result.<br /> <br /> As for the Fate 2 Attainment, yeah, that is a hard one to really consider, at least not automatically since there is no real good way to make that work. I suppose you could put checkboxes, but that is more of a ST decision anyway and this is more for basically players than ST.<br /> <br /> Plus if you really wanted to, you could just add Yantra Bonuses and increase the spell's duration as expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 06-22-2016, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T07:02:44-07:00","id":920940,"title":"","content":"This is awesome. The only thing that I have noticed after last nights' game session - I don't see anywhere to add in additional paradox dice for prior Paradox rolls by same mage in same scene.<br /> If possible it would also be nice if checking the &quot;Instant Cast&quot; &quot;Adv. Duration&quot; etc. boxes at the bottom, would increment the &quot;Reaches&quot; number so that you don't accidentally count them multiple times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980","name":"jmkoontz1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T07:31:17-07:00","id":920947,"title":"","content":"Tested for a bit new version - only some GUI advice:<ul><li>Maybe move 'Reset' and 'Roll This!' button somewhere higher? They are a bit in unintuitive places.</li> <li>Also, Factors categories should over each other - i.e. Potency Factor with Adv. Potency and Potency (Default Factor) , Reaches under Free Reaches, etc.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T15:33:06-07:00","id":921196,"title":"","content":"This is actually awesome. I'll give it a hard try! Thank you very much!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T21:48:50-07:00","id":921342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jmkoontz1980</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/914782-spell-calculator?p=920940#post920940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is awesome. The only thing that I have noticed after last nights' game session - I don't see anywhere to add in additional paradox dice for prior Paradox rolls by same mage in same scene.<br /> If possible it would also be nice if checking the &quot;Instant Cast&quot; &quot;Adv. Duration&quot; etc. boxes at the bottom, would increment the &quot;Reaches&quot; number so that you don't accidentally count them multiple times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12034\" data-vbnamecard=\"12034\">jmkoontz1980</a>,<br /> <br /> I thought about allowing the addition of more paradox die, but since this is something that is typically easily added I felt it was not something critical to casting the spell and is actually handled by the storyteller. I felt that the casting duration/potency/scale and other factors were far more important to include since you need to consult a chart to determine each individual factor versus Paradox is pretty easily remembered with the new rules.<br /> <br /> As for the reaches, when you select Instant Cast and Advanced Duration the Reaches are automatically incremented and factored into whether or not the spell risks paradox. The &quot;Reaches&quot; Counter are for things that are not covered by commonly used reach effects and I felt it would create confusion to add when a user checked &quot;Instant Casting&quot; and so forth to this number because then you would lose track of what additional reaches you were using and you could lower the reach count using the GUI to remove the reaches associated with Instant Casting and Advanced Duration on accident. So, basically, it was a much more ease of use and less human error design to not add the Instant Casting and other effects to the &quot;Reaches&quot; Counter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:52:56-07:00","id":926514,"title":"","content":"Could you add ability to calculate dice for Combined Spell (basically, add a &quot;Combined Spells&quot; factor, with -2 dice for each) and a line displaying Scale in form of Area/Size, in addition to possible subjects? Other than that, it's pretty much perfect and it really speeds up the game (as I am the only person who memorized factor tables); only thing that popped up was the &quot;I want to cast a combined spell, how do I input that -2 penalty?&quot; and the fact that Rote Quality and 9/8 Again aren't mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-05-2016, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T12:48:12-07:00","id":926571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/914782-spell-calculator?p=926514#post926514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and the fact that Rote Quality and 9/8 Again aren't mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Are these supposed to be exclusive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T12:56:50-07:00","id":926576,"title":"","content":"What I meant to say is that they are mutually exclusive in the calculator (you can't have Rote Quality 9again at the same time), sorry for confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T13:19:25-07:00","id":926591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/914782-spell-calculator?p=926576#post926576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant to say is that they are mutually exclusive in the calculator (you can't have Rote Quality 9again at the same time), sorry for confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does it say you can't have rote quality and 9again at the same time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12014-peraxis","name":"Peraxis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T13:35:47-07:00","id":926602,"title":"","content":"The calculator doesn't allow you to do that. If you pick 9 again and then try to apply Rote Quality, it cancels 9 (or 8) again and applies Rote Quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T15:41:25-07:00","id":926687,"title":"","content":"This IS awesome! But in the spirit of wanting someone else to do all the work for me, I have a Mac, and I'm not about to use BootCamp for this. Is there any chance you can write a version that's OSX- or iOS-friendly? Or host it on a site so everyone can use it in a browser?<br /> <br /> I too thought the masses needed an app for this as soon as I saw the spell process, but I'm a QA tester, not a developer. I can only break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1135-zan","name":"Zan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:52:01-07:00","id":927745,"title":"","content":"Just noticed that the Indefinite button doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8871-griffalo","name":"griffalo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8871_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T13:05:12-07:00","id":927750,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8871-griffalo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8871_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8871\" data-vbnamecard=\"8871\">griffalo</a>,<br /> <br /> It does work if Advanced Duration is applied, which I believe is the intent. I don't believe there is a way to make Indefinite without having Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>,<br /> <br /> I will look into creating a combined spell, though I feel that may in itself be a project of its own since there are a few options you can do with Combined Spells such as having different spell factors for each spell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1135-zan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1135_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1135\" data-vbnamecard=\"1135\">Zan</a><br /> <br /> Have you tried using Mono to run the program?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T10:20:04-08:00","id":1032197,"title":"","content":"Swinging back by to say that this is definitely awesome. Been using it to double check some spell numbers when things got complex in my current game.<br /> 95% usable in its current state, the only real bug is that 9-again/Rote issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T17:04:53-08:00","id":1035526,"title":"","content":"Hey Inodiv,<br /> <br /> Glad this is still working great! What bug do you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T17:47:27-08:00","id":1035553,"title":"","content":"I can't download the calculator at this time, but I will try later. I don't see where it calculates the Casting time. dose it do that. I.E. every Yantra beyond the first ads another turn to the casting time, casting from a grimiore doubles the ritual time, you can get 1 extra dice per casting interval during ritual casting. ETC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T19:30:59-08:00","id":1035587,"title":"","content":"Hey Hardwire99,<br /> <br /> No, it does not currently calculate casting time, just the spell casting factors at the moment. Try this link: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/sh/4697fb2oy089os1/AAC3Ar5GvTQ0mNXCUyfCVGgfa?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/sh/4697fb2oy...UyfCVGgfa?dl=0</a><br /> <br /> That one should work","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T21:32:55-08:00","id":1035617,"title":"","content":"This is great, I was thinking about something like this during our last session, thanks so much for sharing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T00:47:24-08:00","id":1035653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/914782-spell-calculator?p=1035587#post1035587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Hardwire99,<br /> <br /> No, it does not currently calculate casting time, just the spell casting factors at the moment. Try this link: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/sh/4697fb2oy089os1/AAC3Ar5GvTQ0mNXCUyfCVGgfa?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/sh/4697fb2oy...UyfCVGgfa?dl=0</a><br /> <br /> That one should work</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks got it now. It is a very nice program and the 9-Again, 8-Again and Rote Quality all seem to be working for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T02:10:56-08:00","id":1035663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/914782-spell-calculator?p=1035526#post1035526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Inodiv,<br /> <br /> Glad this is still working great! What bug do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the calculator, you can't have 9-again and rote casting both active at the same time. It may also effect 8-again.<br /> <br /> They aren't supposed to be mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T03:05:30-08:00","id":1035666,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that they were mutually exclusive, what makes you think that they are not. In the book it just mentions re-rolling the dice that failed. There is nothing that I see that would state that the Rote Quality can be used with the 8/9-Again qualities. If I missed that then please point it out. The Rote Quality is bad enough without adding the 8/9-Again quality also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T04:41:07-08:00","id":1035677,"title":"","content":"Inodiv is right you can stack 9/8 again on rote quality. I will fix that now and let you know when it is updated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T04:53:02-08:00","id":1035679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/914782-spell-calculator?p=1035666#post1035666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that they were mutually exclusive, what makes you think that they are not. In the book it just mentions re-rolling the dice that failed. There is nothing that I see that would state that the Rote Quality can be used with the 8/9-Again qualities. If I missed that then please point it out. The Rote Quality is bad enough without adding the 8/9-Again quality also.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rote doesn't automatically grant 8/9 again, but if you have abilities that grant both qualities there's absolutely no support in the text for not allowing both to apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T07:04:09-08:00","id":1035700,"title":"","content":"Everyone,<br /> <br /> Here is the new spell calculator that will allow Rote Quality and 9/8 again quality: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/hrgovs6ykd4ia6l/Reach%20Calculator.zip?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/hrgovs6ykd...lator.zip?dl=0</a><br /> <br /> Thanks Inodiv for pointing this out.<br /> <br /> Just an FYI on how this rolling works now is the following:<br /> <br /> 1. It rolls the initial die pool determined by the Arcana level, Gnosis of the caster, and other bonuses<br /> 2. It applies Rote Quality, so it re-rolls all failures<br /> 3. It applies the 9/8 again Quality to all combined rolls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 01-21-2017, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}